        Delivery slices
      </caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Slice</th>
          <th>Scope and dependency</th>
          <th>Evidence</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>1 / Shared mechanics · medium</td>
          <td>
            Implement locked standard-Sun collection, damage and energy costs
            through shared definitions; align game sun identity. Update schemas
            and owning specs. Preserve gravity and handling. Guarantee one
            inherent collector on every ship, with fitted collectors additive.
          </td>
          <td>
            Boundary, collector scaling, resource cap/depletion, damage and
            contact checks; verify production and study parity.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>2 / HUD and field lines · small–medium</td>
          <td>
            Implement the approved line styles, colours, active fills and 2 px
            solar inset through shared HUD rendering. Connect states to real
            collection and damage. Depends on slice 1.
          </td>
          <td>
            Inspect normal, collecting, net-draining, damaging and full-battery
            states in play; verify 1 px strokes and 2 px separation across zoom
            and display density. Maintain keyboard and landscape touch.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>3 / Path support and Lab reference · medium</td>
          <td>
            Generalize energy fields into the shared Path configuration and
            write the standard-Sun article from the retained decisions. Depends
            on the shared mechanics; does not require new stellar artwork.
          </td>
          <td>
            Schema validation, synchronized readings and unchanged motion for
            energy-only comparisons; article checked against implemented
            behaviour.
          </td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      The wider stellar research and standard-Sun artwork/effects are deferred.
      Neither expands this patch. Readiness and scope are finalized for the
      approved standard-Sun model. Implementation is separate work; this handoff
      does not claim completed integration, gameplay verification or
      publication.
    </p>
